# Pixel-perfect quality

Rendered output must be exact: correct markdown, intentional spacing, stable layout, and Core Web Vitals in the "good" range. Inspect in the browser; do not assume correct source equals correct render.

Complements `frontend-quality.mdc` (production baseline), `responsive-art-director` (breakpoint art direction), and `visual-qa-critic` (creative QA). This rule owns **layout precision, markdown integrity, and performance metrics**.

## Auto-implementation (no separate prompt)

When touching CSS, layout, markdown/MDX content, or customer-facing pages:

1. Invoke `layout-perfection-critic` before marking work done
2. Fix markdown, spacing, and CWV issues in the **same session**, without waiting for the user to ask
3. Do not ship visual or content changes that fail the checklists below

## Markdown (never broken)

Applies to rendered markdown and MDX: docs, legal, blog, in-app rich text, README on public surfaces.

**Must render correctly:**

| Element | Standard |
| --- | --- |
| Headings | Proper hierarchy; no skipped levels; spacing above/below consistent |
| Paragraphs | Readable measure; no collapsed or double-stacked margins |
| Lists | Correct bullets/numbers; nested indent aligned; no broken markers |
| Links | Visible, tappable, underline or clear affordance; external links open appropriately |
| Code inline | Distinct from body; does not break line height |
| Code blocks | Horizontal scroll only inside block; no page overflow; syntax legible |
| Blockquotes | Indented or bordered per design system; not confused with body |
| Tables | Scroll container on mobile if needed; headers aligned; no crushed columns |
| Images | Alt text; max-width constrained; no layout blowout |
| HR / dividers | Intentional spacing; not doubling with section padding |
| Bold / italic | Renders; does not break wrapping |

**Forbidden:**

- Raw markdown syntax visible to users (`**`, `##`, unrendered links)
- Broken list nesting or orphan bullets
- Code blocks causing horizontal page scroll
- Tables overflowing viewport without scroll treatment
- Heading styles that collide with page H1 (duplicate visual weight)
- Prose styles that fight app layout (wrong font, wrong color token)

Use a shared prose class or component (e.g. `.prose`, `MarkdownContent`) everywhere markdown renders. Do not one-off style each page.

## Spacing, padding, and CSS discipline

**Use the design system scale.** Spacing comes from tokens, not random values.

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Token-only spacing | Prefer scale steps (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64…) unless documented exception |
| No magic numbers | Avoid one-off `13px`, `17px`, `23px` without reason in `visual-decisions.md` |
| Consistent padding | Same component type = same padding across routes |
| Alignment | Icons, labels, and baselines align on shared grid |
| Radius and border | Per `design-system-engineer`; no drift between instances |
| Gaps | `gap` in flex/grid matches vertical rhythm of stacked sections |
| Margin collapse | Account for collapsed margins in section spacing |
| Full-bleed | Intentional only; no accidental negative margin hacks |

**Pixel-perfect means intentional**, not obsessive subpixel tweaking on every element. It means:

- No accidental misalignment (1–2px icon drift, uneven card padding)
- No overlapping text and controls
- No clipped content at any required breakpoint
- No horizontal overflow at 360px

## Mobile and desktop optimization

Test at: 1440, 1280, 1024, 768, 430, 390, 360 (see `frontend-quality.mdc`).

| Check | Mobile | Desktop |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Touch targets | ≥ 44px where practical | Hover states where applicable |
| Typography | Rewrapped, not shrink-only | Measure and hierarchy preserved |
| Spacing | Tighter scale allowed; not cramped | Breathing room per art direction |
| Fixed/sticky | Does not cover CTAs or inputs | Does not break scroll rhythm |
| Images | Correct src sizing; no oversized downloads | Sharp, not over-served |
| Forms | Inputs full width; labels visible | Logical column width |

Invoke `responsive-art-director` when composition changes per breakpoint, not only spacing tweaks.

## Core Web Vitals (targets)

Measure on **mobile** (primary Google ranking signal) and spot-check desktop. Use Lighthouse, PageSpeed Insights, or Web Vitals extension on real pages.

| Metric | Good target | Action if worse |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **LCP** (Largest Contentful Paint) | ≤ 2.5s | Optimize hero image/font, reduce blocking JS, preload LCP asset |
| **INP** (Interaction to Next Paint) | ≤ 200ms | Reduce main-thread work, debounce handlers, simplify animations |
| **CLS** (Cumulative Layout Shift) | ≤ 0.1 | Width/height on images, reserve space for fonts and dynamic UI |

**Required practices:**

- Set explicit `width` and `height` (or aspect-ratio) on images and embeds
- `font-display: swap` with metric-matched fallbacks
- No injecting content above existing content without reserved space
- Lazy-load below-fold images; do not lazy-load LCP image
- Prefer CSS transform/opacity for animation
- Split heavy JS; no unnecessary client components on static marketing pages
- Preconnect to font and analytics origins when used

Do not ship public pages with CWV in "needs improvement" or "poor" without documented exception in `critique-log.md`.

## Before merge (checklist)

- [ ] All markdown surfaces render without raw syntax or layout breaks
- [ ] Spacing uses tokens; no visual padding drift between same components
- [ ] No horizontal overflow at 360px
- [ ] Screenshots inspected at required breakpoints
- [ ] LCP, INP, CLS measured on changed public routes (mobile)
- [ ] No new layout shift from images, fonts, or dynamic inserts
- [ ] `layout-perfection-critic` skill run and logged if issues found

